// The common blue 16x2 parallel character LCD module (1602A) with a 16-pin male header, as
// starter kits ship it. Seated frame: z = 0 is the header plastic's underside, so the board's
// underside is at z = 2.54 and its top at z = 4.14. Board, holes and header positions are the
// Vishay LCD-016N002B drawing (Document Number 37295, p. 2), centred on the origin with the
// header along the top edge. The pins are the sheet's p. 2 order. The HD44780U runs on its own
// bus, 4-bit or 8-bit, as LiquidCrystal drives it. A and K are the backlight LED alone: the
// sheet's A pin takes 4.2 V for the LED with its on-board resistor at 0 ohm, so the circuit
// brings its own series resistor. V0 is the far end of the controller's bias ladder, which
// holds an open V0 at VDD, so the glass stays blank until V0 is brought down toward VSS.
